{
  "_comment": "Hostile values through the engine's own reader and input checks, against the machine in hostile.ir.json (one state S, every context field nullable; each trigger Set<X> takes the one field x and sets it, AtLeast and Zero guard a number). A 'stored' case rehydrates the text {\"machine\":\"hostile\",\"version\":1,\"state\":\"S\",\"context\":<stored>}; an 'input' case advances {\"machine\":\"hostile\",\"version\":1,\"state\":\"S\",\"context\":{}} on 'trigger' with 'input'. 'expect' is the context part of the canonical wire after it, or the refusal code. A value no JSON line carries (a lone surrogate in an input) has no input case here: the canonical-wire vectors give it as UTF-16 code units. Every engine reads this file; add a hostile value here, not in one engine's tests.",
  "machine": "hostile",
  "stored": [
    {"name": "number -0 reads as 0", "stored": "{\"n\":-0}", "expect": "{\"n\":0}"},
    {"name": "number -0.0 reads as 0", "stored": "{\"n\":-0.0}", "expect": "{\"n\":0}"},
    {"name": "number 4.5 stays 4.5", "stored": "{\"n\":4.5}", "expect": "{\"n\":4.5}"},
